					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "NONE\n\nThe None node takes a collection of booleans and outputs true if all booleans in the collection are false.\nThis node lives in the same family as the Any and All nodes which output true when any value in the collection is true or when all the values in the collection are true.\n\nExample: The two Bool in nodes go into the Join to create a collection, an array, of booleans. These are tested by None, Any and All. The results change the colors of the rectanges to visualize the false(red) or true(green). Click on the toggle boxes in the Bool In node to see the different behaviors and note that None and All can never be true at the same time due to their conditions."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 222,
					"width": 717,
					"x": 174,
